    <string name="chain_help">Phone → entry → landing → destination. The public IP is the landing hop. The entry is only the first hop.</string>
    <string name="chain_help_action">About</string>
    <string name="chain_help_title">Chain proxy</string>
    <string name="chain_help_body">1. Entry: a group, node, or subscription in the profile selected above. Do not use the catch-all group. The entry is only the first hop and is never the exit IP.\n2. Landing: the exit IP. Pick another group or node in this profile, or one from another profile. The list is grouped by profile.\n3. Save binds only the profile selected at the top. Each profile keeps its own landing. Switching profiles uses that profile’s own chain.\n4. The choice stays on this phone. It is not written into the subscription, and refreshing the subscription does not clear it.\n5. This uses the built-in dialer-proxy. Path: phone → entry → landing → destination. There is no second protocol stack.\n6. If the chain cannot be built, startup stops with an error. It does not silently fall through to DIRECT.\n7. Use rule mode. Traffic that is not China or private is sent to the landing. China, LAN, and reject rules stay. DNS is not moved onto the chain.\n8. Rules that pointed at the entry are rewritten to the landing, so the exit is not the entry.</string>
